    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression \\(2x + 5\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   2(3) + 5\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the value inside the parentheses:**\n\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 3 = 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6 + 5 = 11\n   \\]\n\n   So, \\(2x + 5\\) evaluates to 11 when \\(x = 3\\).\n\n3. **Square the result:**\n\n   \\[\n   (2x + 5)^2 = 11^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   11^2 = 121\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
